From: Coram Engineering <eng@coram.ai>
Subject: [PATCH] fmp4mux: fix deadlock when all streams have late GOPs

In chunk mode the per-stream fill check marks a stream as filled and sets
late_gop when its oldest queued GOP starts after the current fragment end,
which makes drain_buffers_one_stream() return no buffers for it.

The aggregate decision that selects which stream's fragment_filled flag to
trust used the exact negation of that condition: it only considered streams
whose oldest queued GOP starts at or before the fragment end (or begins with
a non-keyframe). When every stream is in the late-GOP state, find() returns
None, the fragment is never considered filled and fragment_start_pts is never
advanced. Since no GOP can start at or before a fragment end that never moves,
the muxer can never recover: it keeps opening new chunks, draining zero
buffers, and queueing input indefinitely.

This is reachable whenever the encoder GOP duration is close to
fragment-duration: the fragment boundary drifts through the GOP and eventually
lands just before a GOP start (observed at 0.6ms), after which live output
stops permanently with >60s of GOPs queued and growing.

Allow a stream in the late-GOP state to be selected so the aggregate agrees
with the per-stream decision and the fragment can be advanced.
diff --git a/mux/fmp4/src/fmp4mux/imp.rs b/mux/fmp4/src/fmp4mux/imp.rs
index 50750c69..f8954d02 100644
--- a/mux/fmp4/src/fmp4mux/imp.rs
+++ b/mux/fmp4/src/fmp4mux/imp.rs
@@ -2651,8 +2651,14 @@ impl FMP4Mux {
                     .iter()
                     .find(|s| {
                         !s.sinkpad.is_eos()
-                            && s.queued_gops.back().is_some_and(|gop| {
-                                gop.start_pts <= fragment_end_pts
+                            // A stream whose queued GOPs all start after the fragment end has
+                            // already marked itself filled via the late-GOP path and will drain
+                            // nothing. It must still be eligible here, otherwise no stream is
+                            // selected, the fragment is never considered filled and can never be
+                            // advanced - deadlocking the muxer with data queued forever.
+                            && (s.late_gop
+                                || s.queued_gops.back().is_some_and(|gop| {
+                                    gop.start_pts <= fragment_end_pts
                                 // In chunk mode we might've drained a partial GOP as a chunk after
                                 // the fragment end if the keyframe came too late. The GOP now
                                 // starts with a non-keyframe after the fragment end but is part of
@@ -2661,7 +2667,7 @@ impl FMP4Mux {
                                 || gop.buffers.first().is_some_and(|b| {
                                     b.buffer.flags().contains(gst::BufferFlags::DELTA_UNIT)
                                 })
-                            })
+                                }))
                     })
                     .is_some_and(|s| s.fragment_filled)
         };
